</g></svg><div class="scroll" role="region" tabindex="0" aria-label="Domains"><table class="list"><caption>Domains</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Domain</th><th scope="col">Records</th><th scope="col">Question</th><th scope="col">Example in this model</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Customer</td><td>Need (<code>need.<wbr></code>), constraint (<code>constraint.<wbr></code>)</td><td>What does the customer want? What limits the answer?</td><td>{{if .Guide.Need}}{{inline .Guide.Need}}{{else}}{{gap "None"}}{{end}}</td></tr><tr><td>Functional</td><td>Functional requirement (<code>fr.<wbr></code>), criterion</td><td>What must the product do, and how do we accept it?</td><td>{{if .Guide.FR}}{{inline .Guide.FR}}{{else}}{{gap "None"}}{{end}}</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Design parameter (<code>dp.<wbr></code>)</td><td>Which design choice controls each FR?</td><td>{{if .Guide.DP}}{{inline .Guide.DP}}{{else}}{{gap "None"}}{{end}}</td></tr><tr><td>Process</td><td>Process variable (<code>pv.<wbr></code>), module, flow</td><td>How do we build and run each DP?</td><td>{{if .Guide.Process}}{{inline .Guide.Process}}{{else}}{{gap "None"}}{{end}}</td></tr></tbody></table></div></section>
<section class="block" id="g-axioms" aria-labelledby="g-ax-h"><h2 id="g-ax-h">The two axioms</h2><div class="guide-grid"><div><h3>1. Independence Axiom</h3><p>Keep the FRs independent of each other. Each DP must change its own FR and, at most, FRs that you set later. Then you can adjust one outcome without breaking another.</p></div><div><h3>2. Information Axiom</h3><p>Among the designs that keep the FRs independent, select the design with the highest probability of meeting the requirements. This needs evidence, for example trial results.</p></div></div></section>
<section class="block" id="g-matrix" aria-labelledby="g-mx-h"><h2 id="g-mx-h">How to read a design matrix</h2><p class="lede">Rows are FRs and columns are DPs. Each DP sits in the column under the FR that it controls, so the diagonal pairs each FR with its DP. The shape of the matrix gives the classification.</p><div class="scroll" role="region" tabindex="0" aria-label="Matrix symbols"><table class="list"><caption>Matrix symbols</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Symbol</th><th scope="col">Meaning</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><table class="matrix"><tr><td class="x">X</td></tr></table></td><td>The DP changes the FR. The effect is material.</td></tr><tr><td><table class="matrix"><tr><td class="x off">X</td></tr></table></td><td>The DP changes an FR that it does not control. This cell is off the diagonal.</td></tr><tr><td><table class="matrix"><tr><td class="zero">0</td></tr></table></td><td>The DP does not change the FR.</td></tr><tr><td><table class="matrix"><tr><td class="unk">?</td></tr></table></td><td>The model declares no effect. The tool cannot rule one out.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<div class="views examples"><div><h3>{{cls "uncoupled"}}</h3><table class="matrix"><thead><tr><th></th><th scope="col">DP1</th><th scope="col">DP2</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">FR1</th><td class="x">X</td><td class="zero">0</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">FR2</th><td class="zero">0</td><td class="x">X</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Diagonal. Set the DPs in any order. This is the best case.</p></div><div><h3>{{cls "decoupled"}}</h3><table class="matrix"><thead><tr><th></th><th scope="col">DP1</th><th scope="col">DP2</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">FR1</th><td class="x">X</td><td class="zero">0</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">FR2</th><td class="x off">X</td><td class="x">X</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Triangular. Set DP1 first, then DP2. The design stays independent.</p></div><div><h3>{{cls "coupled"}}</h3><table class="matrix"><thead><tr><th></th><th scope="col">DP1</th><th scope="col">DP2</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">FR1</th><td class="x">X</td><td class="x off">X</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">FR2</th><td class="x off">X</td><td class="x">X</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Other shapes. A change to one DP moves both FRs. Tuning can repeat.</p></div><div><h3>{{cls "unresolved"}}</h3><table class="matrix"><thead><tr><th></th><th scope="col">DP1</th><th scope="col">DP2</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">FR1</th><td class="x">X</td><td class="unk">?</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">FR2</th><td class="unk">?</td><td class="x">X</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Unknown cells. Declare them before the tool can classify.</p></div></div></section>
<section class="block" id="g-labels" aria-labelledby="g-lab-h"><h2 id="g-lab-h">Labels on this page</h2><p class="lede">Each claim carries a label that says where it comes from.</p><div class="scroll" role="region" tabindex="0" aria-label="Labels"><table class="list"><caption>Labels</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Label</th><th scope="col">Meaning</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>{{tag (label "source")}}</td><td>The model states this. The location gives the file and the line.</td></tr><tr><td>{{tag (label "inferred")}}</td><td>The model states this, and the author marks it as an inference, not a fact from the source.</td></tr><tr><td>{{tag (label "tool")}}</td><td>The adhcl tool assessed this from the model.</td></tr><tr><td>{{tag (label "derived")}}</td><td>The page follows model links to show this, for example a need that a child FR inherits from its parent.</td></tr><tr><td>{{tag (label "gap")}}</td><td>The model has no record for this. It is a gap, not a zero.</td></tr></tbody></table></div></section>
<section class="block" id="g-ids" aria-labelledby="g-id-h"><h2 id="g-id-h">ID prefixes</h2><p class="lede">The prefix of an ID gives the kind of record. The alias, for example FR11, is the ID from the source document.</p><div class="scroll" role="region" tabindex="0" aria-label="ID prefixes"><table class="list"><caption>ID prefixes</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Prefix</th><th scope="col">Record</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>design.<wbr></code></td><td>The design and its boundary</td></tr><tr><td><code>stakeholder.<wbr></code></td><td>Person or group that the product affects</td></tr><tr><td><code>need.<wbr></code></td><td>Need of a stakeholder</td></tr><tr><td><code>constraint.<wbr></code></td><td>Limit on acceptable solutions</td></tr><tr><td><code>fr.<wbr></code></td><td>Functional requirement</td></tr><tr><td><code>fr.<wbr>NAME.<wbr>criterion.<wbr></code></td><td>Acceptance criterion of one FR</td></tr><tr><td><code>dp.<wbr></code></td><td>Design parameter</td></tr><tr><td><code>pv.<wbr></code></td><td>Process variable</td></tr><tr><td><code>module.<wbr></code></td><td>Software module</td></tr><tr><td><code>flow.<wbr></code></td><td>Order in which modules run</td></tr><tr><td><code>state.<wbr></code></td><td>Information that a DP owns or reads</td></tr><tr><td><code>assumption.<wbr></code></td><td>Premise of the design</td></tr><tr><td><code>context.<wbr></code>, <code>workload.<wbr></code></td><td>Operating condition</td></tr><tr><td><code>decision.<wbr></code></td><td>Choice between candidates</td></tr><tr><td><code>coupling.<wbr></code></td><td>Record of a coupling that the team keeps</td></tr><tr><td><code>expect.<wbr></code></td><td>Expected classification</td></tr><tr><td><code>scenario.<wbr></code></td><td>Test of one or more criteria</td></tr><tr><td><code>evidence.<wbr></code></td><td>Recorded trial result</td></tr><tr><td><code>source.<wbr></code></td><td>Cited document</td></tr></tbody></table></div></section>
<section class="block" id="g-codes" aria-labelledby="g-codes-h"><h2 id="g-codes-h">Finding codes</h2><p class="lede">The tool reports these codes for this model. A warning does not stop the assessment. An error does.</p>{{with .Codes}}<div class="scroll" role="region" tabindex="0" aria-label="{{plural (len .) "code" "codes"}} in this model"><table class="list"><caption>{{plural (len .) "code" "codes"}} in this model</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Code</th><th scope="col">Meaning</th><th scope="col">What to do</th></tr></thead><tbody>{{range .}}<tr id="code.{{.Code}}"><td><code>{{wbr .Code}}</code></td><td>{{.Meaning}}</td><td>{{.Action}}</td></tr>{{end}}</tbody></table></div>{{else}}<p>{{none "The tool reported no findings for this model."}}</p>{{end}}</section>
<section class="block" id="g-terms" aria-labelledby="g-terms-h"><h2 id="g-terms-h">Other terms</h2><div class="scroll" role="region" tabindex="0" aria-label="Other terms"><table class="list"><caption>Other terms</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Term</th><th scope="col">Meaning</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Leaf</td><td>An FR or DP with no children. Modules realize leaf DPs.</td></tr><tr><td>Sibling set</td><td>The FRs and DPs directly under one parent DP. Each set has one matrix.</td></tr><tr><td>Master matrix</td><td>One matrix of all leaf FRs and all leaf DPs.</td></tr><tr><td>Design order</td><td>The order in which to set the DPs of a decoupled matrix.</td></tr><tr><td>Candidate</td><td>One alternative set of DPs in a decision.</td></tr><tr><td>Provisional</td><td>Selected for now, with evidence still missing.</td></tr><tr><td>Junction</td><td>How modules join: S (summation, any order), C (control, fixed order), F (feedback, repeat).</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p class="none cite">Source: N. P. Suh, Axiomatic Design: Advances and Applications (2001).{{range .Sources}} The model cites <a class="ref" href="#{{.ID}}"><code>{{wbr .ID}}</code></a>, {{.Text}}.{{end}}</p></section></section>
